{"text": "To target 24 using the numbers [1, 1, 2, 6] each exactly once with the operations +, -, *, /, we can use the following combination:", "start": 0, "end": 131, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "6 × (2 + 1 + (1/1)) = 6 × (2 + 1 + 1) = 6 × 4 = 24", "start": 133, "end": 183, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Here's the breakdown:", "start": 185, "end": 206, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "1. First, add 1 and 1 to get 2.", "start": 207, "end": 238, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "2. Then, take the reciprocal of 1, which is 1.", "start": 239, "end": 285, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "3. Add 2 and 1 to get 3.", "start": 286, "end": 310, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "4. Add another 1 to get 4.", "start": 311, "end": 337, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "5. Finally, multiply 6 by 4 to get 24.", "start": 338, "end": 376, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So, the expression is:", "start": 378, "end": 400, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "6 × (2 + 1 + (1/1)) = 24", "start": 402, "end": 426, "label": "inform"}
